{"toolCallId":"call_16c1985773c04cfb8d870d50bfeb091b","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Variables**: `S` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`. `P` is `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the argument parser and both output functions (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'output_text|output_json|--json\\)' $S` prints the parser case and both function definitions.\n- [ ] T002 Confirm the packet adds no configuration surface (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'CONFIG|\\.conf|env ' $S` prints no configuration read, so the Config phase has nothing to change.\n- [ ] T003 Capture the pre-change default report (`$P/scratch/before.txt`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 500 --files 15 > $P/scratch/before.txt` exits 0 and `wc -l < $P/scratch/before.txt` prints 16.\n- [ ] T004 [P] Capture the pre-change JSON document (`$P/scratch/before.json`). Verify: `bash $S --json --loc 100 --files 3 > $P/scratch/before.json` exits 0 and `head -1 $P/scratch/before.json` prints `{`.\n- [ ] T005 [P] Record the pre-change `--quiet` failure (`$P/scratch/before-quiet.txt`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 2> $P/scratch/before-quiet.txt; echo $?` prints 1 and the file holds `Unknown option: --quiet`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T006 Add `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` to the globals block next to `JSON_OUTPUT` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'QUIET_OUTPUT=false' $S` prints one line.\n- [ ] T007 Add the `--quiet` case to the argument parser (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet\\)' $S` prints the case arm.\n- [ ] T008 Add the quiet guard to the top of `output_text` so it prints the level line and returns (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints `Recommended Level: 2 (Verification)` and nothing else.\n- [ ] T009 Document `--quiet` in the header OPTIONS block and in `show_help` (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --help | rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints 1.\n- [ ] T010 Keep `--json` ahead of the quiet branch in the output dispatch (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --json --loc 100 --files 3 | head -1` prints `{`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T011 Diff the default report against the baseline (`$P/scratch/before.txt`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 500 --files 15 | diff - $P/scratch/before.txt` prints nothing and exits 0.\n- [ ] T012 Diff the JSON document against the baseline (`$P/scratch/before.json`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --json --loc 100 --files 3 | diff - $P/scratch/before.json` prints nothing and exits 0.\n- [ ] T013 Run the four flag combinations with valid input (`$S`). Verify: the matrix rows in `plan.md` each print the expected first line and exit 0.\n- [ ] T014 Run invalid input in text and quiet modes (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet 2>&1; echo $?` prints the existing two-line message and 1.\n- [ ] T015 Run the shell syntax gate (`$S`). Verify: `bash -n $S` exits 0 and prints nothing.\n- [ ] T016 Record the evidence in this file and rerun strict validation (`$P`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh $P --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 | wc -l` prints 1 and both baseline diffs are empty\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See `plan.md` ADR-001 and ADR-002\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## AI Execution Protocol\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\n\nBefore starting any task, verify:\n1. [ ] `spec.md` scope unchanged since this file was written\n2. [ ] Current phase identified in `plan.md` section 4\n3. [ ] Task dependencies satisfied, per the matrix in `plan.md`\n4. [ ] Relevant P0 and P1 checklist items identified\n5. [ ] No blocking issue recorded against ADR-001 or ADR-002\n6. [ ] Previous session context reviewed in `implementation-summary.md`, if one exists\n7. [ ] Baseline captures in `scratch/` still match the current script\n8. [ ] Success criteria SC-001 to SC-004 read and understood\n9. [ ] `bash -n` passes on the current script before any edit\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| TASK-SEQ | Complete tasks in dependency order |\n| TASK-SCOPE | Stay within the task boundary, no adjacent cleanup |\n| TASK-VERIFY | Run the task's `Verify:` command and read its output before marking it done |\n| TASK-DOC | Update task state immediately on completion |\n| TASK-BASELINE | Never edit the script before T003 and T004 have captured both baselines |\n| TASK-QUIET | Keep `--json` ahead of the quiet branch in every dispatch edit |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\n\n```\n## Status Update - [TIMESTAMP]\n- **Task**: T### - [Description]\n- **Status**: [IN_PROGRESS | COMPLETED | BLOCKED]\n- **Evidence**: [Command output, diff result or file path]\n- **Blockers**: [None | Description]\n- **Next**: T### - [Next task]\n```\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\n\nA task becomes `[B]` when its `Verify:` command fails twice for a reason outside the task, or when a dependency task is incomplete. On a block, record the command, its exit code and the failing line in this file, then move to a task that does not depend on it. Do not mark a blocked task `[x]`, and do not claim completion while a `[B]` row remains.\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md. Verify: `rg -c 'REQ-00' spec.md` prints 6.\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach, files and rollback defined in plan.md. Verify: `rg -n 'recommend-level.sh' plan.md` prints at least three lines.\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available. Verify: `bash --version` exits 0 and `command -v diff` prints a path.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] The script passes the shell syntax check. Verify: `bash -n $S` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] A valid run emits no unexpected stderr. Verify: `bash $S --loc 500 --files 15 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Invalid input still exits 1 with the existing message. Verify: `bash $S --quiet 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints `Unknown option: --quiet` before the feature and the no-input message after it.\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The branch matches the existing `if [[ \"$JSON_OUTPUT\" = true ]]` style. Verify: `rg -n 'QUIET_OUTPUT' $S` prints the global, the parser arm and the guard.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met. Verify: every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` reads `Met` with observed evidence.\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Manual matrix complete. Verify: the eight rows in `plan.md` are each run and recorded.\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested. Verify: empty input, maximum input, repeated flag and flag order each print the expected result.\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated. Verify: no input, non-numeric `--loc` and unknown flag each exit 1 with the existing message.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime` names only `recommend-level.sh`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed. Verify: `rg -n 'recommend-level.sh' .skilled/skills --glob '*.md' --glob '*.sh'` lists every caller and doc.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Adversarial rows cover repeated flag, flag order, empty input and non-numeric input.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count listed before completion is claimed. Verify: `plan.md` names four flag combinations and two input states.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile environment variant executed. Verify: `env -i bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints one line and exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence is pinned to a commit SHA or an explicit diff range, not a moving branch-relative range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets. Verify: `rg -n 'token|secret|password' $S` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation unchanged. Verify: `bash $S --loc abc` exits 1 with the existing message.\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] N/A, the script has no auth or authz surface.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec, plan and tasks name the same flag and the same line format. Verify: `rg -c 'Recommended Level: N \\(Name\\)' spec.md plan.md` prints one line per file.\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The header comment and `show_help` both list `--quiet`. Verify: `rg -c -- '--quiet' $S` prints 2 or more.\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] No README outside the script documents this flag. Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit --glob '*.md'` names no other page.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Baseline captures live in `scratch/` only. Verify: `ls $P/scratch` lists `before.txt`, `before.json` and `before-quiet.txt`.\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` is cleaned or kept as evidence at completion, and no capture lands in the repository root.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 15 | 0/15 |\n| P1 Items | 23 | 0/23 |\n| P2 Items | 9 | 0/9 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-26\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is followed by T007 and T008, and ADR-002 by T010.\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] All ADRs have a status. Verify: `rg -n '^\\*\\*Status\\*\\*' plan.md` prints two `Accepted` lines.\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives documented with rejection rationale. Verify: `rg -n 'Alternatives Rejected' plan.md` prints two lines.\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] N/A, the change has no data or config migration path.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] NFR-P01 met. Verify: `/usr/bin/time -p bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints `real 0.00`, the same as the default run.\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] N/A, the script processes one input set per run and has no throughput target.\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] N/A, load testing does not apply to a single-shot CLI.\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] N/A, no benchmark is claimed beyond the timing above.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented and tested. Verify: reverting the commit restores both baseline diffs to empty.\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] N/A, the flag itself is the feature and no separate feature flag exists.\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] N/A, the script emits no metrics and needs no alerting.\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] N/A, `--help` is the runbook for one command.\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] N/A, there is no deployment runbook to review.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] N/A, the change touches no security surface, as `spec.md` section 7 records.\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] N/A, no dependency is added.\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] N/A, the script has no network or input parsing surface in the OWASP sense.\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] N/A, the script stores and transmits no data.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized. Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet' spec.md plan.md tasks.md acceptance-criteria.md` names the same flag in all four.\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] N/A, the script exposes no API beyond its command line.\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated. Verify: `bash $S --help` lists the flag.\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] N/A, the change needs no knowledge transfer beyond this packet.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| Conductor | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| Operator | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| Conductor | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Variables**: `S` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`. `P` is `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the argument parser and both output functions (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'output_text|output_json|--json\\)' $S` prints the parser case and both function definitions.\n- [ ] T002 Confirm the packet adds no configuration surface (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'CONFIG|\\.conf|env ' $S` prints no configuration read, so the Config phase has nothing to change.\n- [ ] T003 Capture the pre-change default report (`$P/scratch/before.txt`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 500 --files 15 > $P/scratch/before.txt` exits 0 and `wc -l < $P/scratch/before.txt` prints 16.\n- [ ] T004 [P] Capture the pre-change JSON document (`$P/scratch/before.json`). Verify: `bash $S --json --loc 100 --files 3 > $P/scratch/before.json` exits 0 and `head -1 $P/scratch/before.json` prints `{`.\n- [ ] T005 [P] Record the pre-change `--quiet` failure (`$P/scratch/before-quiet.txt`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 2> $P/scratch/before-quiet.txt; echo $?` prints 1 and the file holds `Unknown option: --quiet`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T006 Add `QUIET_OUTPUT=false` to the globals block next to `JSON_OUTPUT` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'QUIET_OUTPUT=false' $S` prints one line.\n- [ ] T007 Add the `--quiet` case to the argument parser (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet\\)' $S` prints the case arm.\n- [ ] T008 Add the quiet guard to the top of `output_text` so it prints the level line and returns (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints `Recommended Level: 2 (Verification)` and nothing else.\n- [ ] T009 Document `--quiet` in the header OPTIONS block and in `show_help` (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --help | rg -c -- '--quiet'` prints 1.\n- [ ] T010 Keep `--json` ahead of the quiet branch in the output dispatch (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --json --loc 100 --files 3 | head -1` prints `{`.\n- [ ] T017 Implement REQ-007: confine the quiet guard to stdout and leave fd 2 untouched, so a warning still reaches stderr (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --loc abc 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints `ERROR: --loc requires a numeric value` and `rg -n '2>&1' $S` prints nothing.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T011 Diff the default report against the baseline (`$P/scratch/before.txt`). Verify: `bash $S --loc 500 --files 15 | diff - $P/scratch/before.txt` prints nothing and exits 0.\n- [ ] T012 Diff the JSON document against the baseline (`$P/scratch/before.json`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet --json --loc 100 --files 3 | diff - $P/scratch/before.json` prints nothing and exits 0.\n- [ ] T013 Run the four flag combinations with valid input (`$S`). Verify: the matrix rows in `plan.md` each print the expected first line and exit 0.\n- [ ] T014 Run invalid input in text and quiet modes (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --quiet 2>&1; echo $?` prints the existing two-line message and 1.\n- [ ] T015 Run the shell syntax gate (`$S`). Verify: `bash -n $S` exits 0 and prints nothing.\n- [ ] T016 Record the evidence in this file and rerun strict validation (`$P`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh $P --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15 | wc -l` prints 1 and both baseline diffs are empty\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See `plan.md` ADR-001 and ADR-002\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## AI Execution Protocol\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\n\nBefore starting any task, verify:\n1. [ ] `spec.md` scope unchanged since this file was written\n2. [ ] Current phase identified in `plan.md` section 4\n3. [ ] Task dependencies satisfied, per the matrix in `plan.md`\n4. [ ] Relevant P0 and P1 checklist items identified\n5. [ ] No blocking issue recorded against ADR-001 or ADR-002\n6. [ ] Previous session context reviewed in `implementation-summary.md`, if one exists\n7. [ ] Baseline captures in `scratch/` still match the current script\n8. [ ] Success criteria SC-001 to SC-004 read and understood\n9. [ ] `bash -n` passes on the current script before any edit\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| TASK-SEQ | Complete tasks in dependency order |\n| TASK-SCOPE | Stay within the task boundary, no adjacent cleanup |\n| TASK-VERIFY | Run the task's `Verify:` command and read its output before marking it done |\n| TASK-DOC | Update task state immediately on completion |\n| TASK-BASELINE | Never edit the script before T003 and T004 have captured both baselines |\n| TASK-QUIET | Keep `--json` ahead of the quiet branch in every dispatch edit |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\n\n```\n## Status Update - [TIMESTAMP]\n- **Task**: T### - [Description]\n- **Status**: [IN_PROGRESS | COMPLETED | BLOCKED]\n- **Evidence**: [Command output, diff result or file path]\n- **Blockers**: [None | Description]\n- **Next**: T### - [Next task]\n```\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\n\nA task becomes `[B]` when its `Verify:` command fails twice for a reason outside the task, or when a dependency task is incomplete. On a block, record the command, its exit code and the failing line in this file, then move to a task that does not depend on it. Do not mark a blocked task `[x]`, and do not claim completion while a `[B]` row remains.\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md. Verify: `rg -c 'REQ-00' spec.md` prints 6.\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach, files and rollback defined in plan.md. Verify: `rg -n 'recommend-level.sh' plan.md` prints at least three lines.\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available. Verify: `bash --version` exits 0 and `command -v diff` prints a path.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] The script passes the shell syntax check. Verify: `bash -n $S` exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] A valid run emits no unexpected stderr. Verify: `bash $S --loc 500 --files 15 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] Invalid input still exits 1 with the existing message. Verify: `bash $S --quiet 2>&1 >/dev/null` prints `Unknown option: --quiet` before the feature and the no-input message after it.\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The branch matches the existing `if [[ \"$JSON_OUTPUT\" = true ]]` style. Verify: `rg -n 'QUIET_OUTPUT' $S` prints the global, the parser arm and the guard.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met. Verify: every row in `acceptance-criteria.md` reads `Met` with observed evidence.\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] Manual matrix complete. Verify: the eight rows in `plan.md` are each run and recorded.\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] Edge cases tested. Verify: empty input, maximum input, repeated flag and flag order each print the expected result.\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Error scenarios validated. Verify: no input, non-numeric `--loc` and unknown flag each exit 1 with the existing message.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Each actionable finding has a finding class: `instance-only`, `class-of-bug`, `cross-consumer`, `algorithmic`, `matrix/evidence`, or `test-isolation`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Same-class producer inventory completed. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime` names only `recommend-level.sh`.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P0] Consumer inventory completed. Verify: `rg -n 'recommend-level.sh' .skilled/skills --glob '*.md' --glob '*.sh'` lists every caller and doc.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P0] Adversarial rows cover repeated flag, flag order, empty input and non-numeric input.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix axes and row count listed before completion is claimed. Verify: `plan.md` names four flag combinations and two input states.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-006 [P1] Hostile environment variant executed. Verify: `env -i bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints one line and exits 0.\n- [ ] CHK-FIX-007 [P1] Evidence is pinned to a commit SHA or an explicit diff range, not a moving branch-relative range.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets. Verify: `rg -n 'token|secret|password' $S` prints nothing.\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation unchanged. Verify: `bash $S --loc abc` exits 1 with the existing message.\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] N/A, the script has no auth or authz surface.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] Spec, plan and tasks name the same flag and the same line format. Verify: `rg -c 'Recommended Level: N \\(Name\\)' spec.md plan.md` prints one line per file.\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The header comment and `show_help` both list `--quiet`. Verify: `rg -c -- '--quiet' $S` prints 2 or more.\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] No README outside the script documents this flag. Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet' .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit --glob '*.md'` names no other page.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Baseline captures live in `scratch/` only. Verify: `ls $P/scratch` lists `before.txt`, `before.json` and `before-quiet.txt`.\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` is cleaned or kept as evidence at completion, and no capture lands in the repository root.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 15 | 0/15 |\n| P1 Items | 23 | 0/23 |\n| P2 Items | 9 | 0/9 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-26\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is followed by T007 and T008, and ADR-002 by T010.\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] All ADRs have a status. Verify: `rg -n '^\\*\\*Status\\*\\*' plan.md` prints two `Accepted` lines.\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Alternatives documented with rejection rationale. Verify: `rg -n 'Alternatives Rejected' plan.md` prints two lines.\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] N/A, the change has no data or config migration path.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] NFR-P01 met. Verify: `/usr/bin/time -p bash $S --quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints `real 0.00`, the same as the default run.\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P1] N/A, the script processes one input set per run and has no throughput target.\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] N/A, load testing does not apply to a single-shot CLI.\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] N/A, no benchmark is claimed beyond the timing above.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented and tested. Verify: reverting the commit restores both baseline diffs to empty.\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P0] N/A, the flag itself is the feature and no separate feature flag exists.\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P1] N/A, the script emits no metrics and needs no alerting.\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P1] N/A, `--help` is the runbook for one command.\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] N/A, there is no deployment runbook to review.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] N/A, the change touches no security surface, as `spec.md` section 7 records.\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] N/A, no dependency is added.\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] N/A, the script has no network or input parsing surface in the OWASP sense.\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] N/A, the script stores and transmits no data.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized. Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet' spec.md plan.md tasks.md acceptance-criteria.md` names the same flag in all four.\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] N/A, the script exposes no API beyond its command line.\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated. Verify: `bash $S --help` lists the flag.\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] N/A, the change needs no knowledge transfer beyond this packet.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| Conductor | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| Operator | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| Conductor | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_25308e19c2da4ef3b30af134f41f458d","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Callers that need only the level must parse a 16-line report to read one number. The --quiet flag prints only the recommended-level line and leaves every other mode byte-identical.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag\"\n  - \"add a quiet flag to recommend level sh\"\n  - \"recommend-level quiet output\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.3 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n`recommend-level.sh` prints a 16-line human report for every run. A caller that needs the level alone has to capture and parse the whole report. The `--quiet` flag prints one stable line, `Recommended Level: N (Name)`, and a line count plus a byte diff on the default output prove the change is confined to that branch.\n\n**Key Decisions**: `--quiet` is a text-report modifier rather than a global silence switch (ADR-001), and JSON output stays unchanged under it (ADR-002)\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: Bash 3.2 or newer, which the script already requires\n\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\nCallers that need only the level must parse a 16-line report to read one number. A shell caller using command substitution receives the score, the breakdown and the phase section along with the value it asked for, so it either scrapes line 2 or filters with `sed`. Both approaches break when the report gains a line.\n\n### Purpose\nGive callers one stable line to capture, while every existing invocation keeps its current output byte for byte.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Add `--quiet` to the argument parser in `recommend-level.sh`.\n- Print only `Recommended Level: N (Name)` when `--quiet` is set and `--json` is not.\n- Document the flag in the script header and in `show_help`.\n- Keep the default text report and the JSON document byte-identical.\n- Cover the flag combinations with command-level checks.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Changing the scoring weights, thresholds or level mapping - the feature selects output, it does not change the score.\n- Adding a bare-number mode such as `--level-only` - JSON already serves structured consumers.\n- Editing other spec CLI scripts - each change gets its own packet.\n- Adding a test framework to the script - the verification uses shell commands the repository already has.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Modify | Add flag parsing, one output guard and the help text |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\nREQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | `--quiet` is accepted by the argument parser and a valid run that uses it exits 0. |\n| REQ-002 | With `--quiet` and no `--json`, stdout holds exactly one line, `Recommended Level: N (Name)`, with N and Name taken from the same scoring path as today. |\n| REQ-003 | Without `--quiet`, stdout is unchanged from the pre-change script: same 16 lines, same order, same values, 310 bytes for `--loc 500 --files 15`. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-004 | `--help` lists `--quiet` in its OPTIONS block with a one-line description. |\n| REQ-005 | With `--quiet` and `--json`, the JSON document is unchanged from a `--json`-only run, because JSON mode already emits one structured document. |\n| REQ-006 | `--quiet` leaves stderr diagnostics and exit codes alone: invalid input still prints the existing message and exits 1. |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints one line, `Recommended Level: 2 (Verification)`, and exits 0.\n- **SC-002**: `recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15` produces output identical to the captured baseline, proven by an empty `diff`.\n- **SC-003**: `recommend-level.sh --quiet --json --loc 100 --files 3` produces output identical to `recommend-level.sh --json --loc 100 --files 3`.\n- **SC-004**: `recommend-level.sh --help` names `--quiet` once in the OPTIONS block.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | Bash 3.2 or newer, already required by the script | The script cannot run | No new requirement is introduced, so the fallback is the current interpreter |\n| Risk | A caller parses the level line and breaks when its label changes | Med | REQ-002 fixes the label and AC-002 pins the exact text |\n| Risk | `--quiet` leaks into JSON consumers and changes their document | Med | REQ-005 and AC-005 diff the JSON output against a `--json`-only run |\n| Risk | The help text drifts from the parser | Low | AC-004 reads `--help` and T008 edits both in one task |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: `--quiet` adds no measurable time. The run stays below the 10 ms resolution of `/usr/bin/time -p`, the same as the current script.\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: The script reads no credentials, makes no network calls and writes no files. The flag adds no input that reaches the shell unquoted.\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: Output is deterministic for the same inputs. Repeated runs of the same invocation print identical bytes.\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Empty input: no `--loc` and no `--files` prints the existing two-line stderr message and exits 1 in both text and quiet modes.\n- Maximum length: `--loc 100000 --files 1000` prints the same single line under `--quiet` that the full report names on line 2.\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- External service failure: N/A, the script calls no service.\n- Network timeout: N/A, the script opens no socket.\n\n### State Transitions\n- Partial completion: N/A, the script scores once and exits.\n- Session expiry: N/A, the script holds no session.\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | 22/25 | Files: 1, LOC: ~20, Systems: 1 |\n| Risk | 16/25 | Auth: N, API: N, Breaking: N |\n| Research | 18/20 | Both output functions and the help text must be read before editing |\n| Multi-Agent | 10/15 | Workstreams: 1 |\n| Coordination | 10/15 | Dependencies: 1, the shared output dispatch |\n| **Total** | **76/100** | **Level 3** |\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | A caller depends on the exact 16-line layout of the default report | M | L | AC-003 diffs the default output against the captured baseline |\n| R-002 | The flag is wired into JSON mode and changes a machine contract | M | L | AC-005 diffs the JSON document against a `--json`-only run |\n| R-003 | `--quiet` is accepted in one flag position and rejected in another | L | M | AC-001 and T013 exercise order and repetition |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n\n### US-001: One line for a build script (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** build script that needs the level, **I want** a single parseable line, **so that** I can read the value without parsing the report.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: A discoverable flag (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** maintainer reading `--help`, **I want** `--quiet` listed with its effect, **so that** I can use it without reading the source.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- None. `--quiet` suppresses the whole text report, so it needs no interaction with `--no-recommend-phases`.\n- Should a future `--level-only` print the bare number? Not in this packet. JSON covers structured consumers today.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See `plan.md` ADR-001 and ADR-002\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Callers that need only the level must parse a 16-line report to read one number. The --quiet flag prints only the recommended-level line and leaves every other mode byte-identical.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag\"\n  - \"add a quiet flag to recommend level sh\"\n  - \"recommend-level quiet output\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core + level2-verify + level3-arch | v2.3 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n\n---\n\n## EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\n\n`recommend-level.sh` prints a 16-line human report for every run. A caller that needs the level alone has to capture and parse the whole report. The `--quiet` flag prints one stable line, `Recommended Level: N (Name)`, and a line count plus a byte diff on the default output prove the change is confined to that branch.\n\n**Key Decisions**: `--quiet` is a text-report modifier rather than a global silence switch (ADR-001), and JSON output stays unchanged under it (ADR-002)\n\n**Critical Dependencies**: Bash 3.2 or newer, which the script already requires\n\n---\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 3 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\nCallers that need only the level must parse a 16-line report to read one number. A shell caller using command substitution receives the score, the breakdown and the phase section along with the value it asked for, so it either scrapes line 2 or filters with `sed`. Both approaches break when the report gains a line.\n\n### Purpose\nGive callers one stable line to capture, while every existing invocation keeps its current output byte for byte.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Add `--quiet` to the argument parser in `recommend-level.sh`.\n- Print only `Recommended Level: N (Name)` when `--quiet` is set and `--json` is not.\n- Document the flag in the script header and in `show_help`.\n- Keep the default text report and the JSON document byte-identical.\n- Cover the flag combinations with command-level checks.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Changing the scoring weights, thresholds or level mapping - the feature selects output, it does not change the score.\n- Adding a bare-number mode such as `--level-only` - JSON already serves structured consumers.\n- Editing other spec CLI scripts - each change gets its own packet.\n- Adding a test framework to the script - the verification uses shell commands the repository already has.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh` | Modify | Add flag parsing, one output guard and the help text |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\nREQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | `--quiet` is accepted by the argument parser and a valid run that uses it exits 0. |\n| REQ-002 | With `--quiet` and no `--json`, stdout holds exactly one line, `Recommended Level: N (Name)`, with N and Name taken from the same scoring path as today. |\n| REQ-003 | Without `--quiet`, stdout is unchanged from the pre-change script: same 16 lines, same order, same values, 310 bytes for `--loc 500 --files 15`. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-004 | `--help` lists `--quiet` in its OPTIONS block with a one-line description. |\n| REQ-005 | With `--quiet` and `--json`, the JSON document is unchanged from a `--json`-only run, because JSON mode already emits one structured document. |\n| REQ-006 | `--quiet` leaves stderr diagnostics and exit codes alone: invalid input still prints the existing message and exits 1. |\n| REQ-007 | With `--quiet`, any warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr: the flag trims stdout only and never redirects, merges or suppresses fd 2. |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints one line, `Recommended Level: 2 (Verification)`, and exits 0.\n- **SC-002**: `recommend-level.sh --loc 500 --files 15` produces output identical to the captured baseline, proven by an empty `diff`.\n- **SC-003**: `recommend-level.sh --quiet --json --loc 100 --files 3` produces output identical to `recommend-level.sh --json --loc 100 --files 3`.\n- **SC-004**: `recommend-level.sh --help` names `--quiet` once in the OPTIONS block.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | Bash 3.2 or newer, already required by the script | The script cannot run | No new requirement is introduced, so the fallback is the current interpreter |\n| Risk | A caller parses the level line and breaks when its label changes | Med | REQ-002 fixes the label and AC-002 pins the exact text |\n| Risk | `--quiet` leaks into JSON consumers and changes their document | Med | REQ-005 and AC-005 diff the JSON output against a `--json`-only run |\n| Risk | The help text drifts from the parser | Low | AC-004 reads `--help` and T008 edits both in one task |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n## 7. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n### Performance\n- **NFR-P01**: `--quiet` adds no measurable time. The run stays below the 10 ms resolution of `/usr/bin/time -p`, the same as the current script.\n\n### Security\n- **NFR-S01**: The script reads no credentials, makes no network calls and writes no files. The flag adds no input that reaches the shell unquoted.\n\n### Reliability\n- **NFR-R01**: Output is deterministic for the same inputs. Repeated runs of the same invocation print identical bytes.\n\n---\n\n## 8. EDGE CASES\n\n### Data Boundaries\n- Empty input: no `--loc` and no `--files` prints the existing two-line stderr message and exits 1 in both text and quiet modes.\n- Maximum length: `--loc 100000 --files 1000` prints the same single line under `--quiet` that the full report names on line 2.\n\n### Error Scenarios\n- External service failure: N/A, the script calls no service.\n- Network timeout: N/A, the script opens no socket.\n\n### State Transitions\n- Partial completion: N/A, the script scores once and exits.\n- Session expiry: N/A, the script holds no session.\n\n---\n\n## 9. COMPLEXITY ASSESSMENT\n\n| Dimension | Score | Triggers |\n|-----------|-------|----------|\n| Scope | 22/25 | Files: 1, LOC: ~20, Systems: 1 |\n| Risk | 16/25 | Auth: N, API: N, Breaking: N |\n| Research | 18/20 | Both output functions and the help text must be read before editing |\n| Multi-Agent | 10/15 | Workstreams: 1 |\n| Coordination | 10/15 | Dependencies: 1, the shared output dispatch |\n| **Total** | **76/100** | **Level 3** |\n\n---\n\n## 10. RISK MATRIX\n\n| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation |\n|---------|-------------|--------|------------|------------|\n| R-001 | A caller depends on the exact 16-line layout of the default report | M | L | AC-003 diffs the default output against the captured baseline |\n| R-002 | The flag is wired into JSON mode and changes a machine contract | M | L | AC-005 diffs the JSON document against a `--json`-only run |\n| R-003 | `--quiet` is accepted in one flag position and rejected in another | L | M | AC-001 and T013 exercise order and repetition |\n\n---\n\n## 11. USER STORIES\n\n### US-001: One line for a build script (Priority: P0)\n\n**As a** build script that needs the level, **I want** a single parseable line, **so that** I can read the value without parsing the report.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n### US-002: A discoverable flag (Priority: P1)\n\n**As a** maintainer reading `--help`, **I want** `--quiet` listed with its effect, **so that** I can use it without reading the source.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:** see `acceptance-criteria.md` (rows referencing this story).\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 12. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- None. `--quiet` suppresses the whole text report, so it needs no interaction with `--no-recommend-phases`.\n- Should a future `--level-only` print the bare number? Not in this packet. JSON covers structured consumers today.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n## RELATED DOCUMENTS\n\n- **Implementation Plan**: See `plan.md`\n- **Task Breakdown**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Verification Checklist**: See `tasks.md`\n- **Decision Records**: See `plan.md` ADR-001 and ADR-002\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
